      "writtenOn": "2022-09-06T16:55:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You\u0027re right - testing it in https://pl.kotl.in/wld4_ibfx confirms that we block until all the tasks complete.\n\nHowever, go/kotlin/practices/coroutines#api-design suggests that we should avoid what the stdlib does here. The implementor can always wrap their code in a `coroutineScope { }` if they really want to launch tasks and stuff before the scope completes.\n\nWhat do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "27457af6_fdc5c4a5",
      "revId": "7bdb42a6338404631bb9766212a075786c68ebab",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
